      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "util-linux enters the image through the Debian base only; the entrypoint is the Vulnlog native binary, which links just libc and libz and never invokes `mount(8)`. The attack needs an `/etc/fstab` entry combining `user` with `X-mount.owner`, `X-mount.group` or `X-mount.mode`, and the image ships an unconfigured fstab with no entries at all.",
      "supplier": "Vulnlog"
